  "observations": [
    "All four recorded Windows jobs completed with failure on the exact source commit and workflow run. The cached workflow run was still in progress; this proof does not claim a terminal overall run conclusion.",
    "Both native identity jobs reported native-open=false, access-denied=false, invalid-parameter=true and name-invalid=false at the drive-root NtCreateFile call.",
    "Borrowed file identity reached the native fixture assertions; write-only/append-only borrowed-output and thread-impersonation refusal markers passed on both architectures. Positive pathname probes failed.",
    "The dedicated identity step failed before protected storage qualification; that later step was skipped.",
    "Only allowlisted PASS/FAIL test markers and fixed boolean root diagnostics are exported. Raw logs, pathname errors, identities, credentials and private payloads remain excluded."
  ],
  "candidateCorrection": "The root open combines FILE_DIRECTORY_FILE with FILE_OPEN_NO_RECALL. Microsoft MS-FSA excludes NO_RECALL from the permitted DIRECTORY_FILE options; the Cygwin upstream fix records STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER for that combination. Use a type-neutral metadata open retaining FILE_OPEN_NO_RECALL, FILE_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT and FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT, then retain the existing postopen Directory check. A fresh source-bound hosted run is required to verify the correction.",
  "causeEvidence": {
    "observedStatus": "STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER",
    "incompatibleCreateOptions": [
      "FILE_DIRECTORY_FILE",
      "FILE_OPEN_NO_RECALL"
    ],
